# Every package's `format` script loads this file explicitly with --ignore-path,
# because Prettier only auto-discovers a .prettierignore in its own CWD and never
# walks up to the workspace root. Keep patterns `**/`-anchored so they match the
# same way whether Prettier runs from here or from a package directory.

**/package-lock.json
**/pnpm-lock.yaml
**/yarn.lock
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/routeTree.gen.ts
**/.kysely-codegenrc.json
**/modules/data/db.ts
**/*.mp3

# Prose, wrapped by hand and argued over line by line. Prettier reflows it and
# rewrites its tables, so a one-paragraph edit to a decision doc arrives as a
# hundred lines of churn over text nobody touched. None of it has ever been
# formatted — `--check` fails on files that have been correct for months — so
# this records the existing state rather than changing anything.
#
# It was `**/docs/` alone, which stated the rule and then applied it to one
# directory. Every CLAUDE.md, every README and every skill in this repo is the
# same hand-wrapped prose written under the same 100-column habit, and measuring
# it bore the argument out exactly: Prettier repads the module table in
# `apps/api/README.md`, rewrites the destination table at the top of `CLAUDE.md`,
# and reformats the illustrative JSON inside `analysis/README.md` — including
# adding a trailing comma to a block that has `//` comments in it and was never
# JSON. Eleven files and 333 lines of churn over text nobody had touched.
**/docs/
**/*.md

# Written by a tool rather than by anybody, and rewritten every time the tool
# runs. Formatting it is a diff that comes back.
**/.claude/settings.local.json

# The contracts, and this one is a measurement rather than a preference. The
# ContractKit plugin loads and will happily rewrite these, and what it produces
# is worse than what is here on every file it touches:
#
#   - a standalone comment ABOVE a field is hoisted onto the end of that field's
#     line, which is where most of these already put their documentation and is
#     the reason the lines are long in the first place;
#   - printWidth counts that trailing comment, so the formatter then breaks the
#     only breakable thing left. `kind?: enum(host, caller)` with a 200-character
#     doc comment after it becomes a three-line enum.
#
# 29 lines of `personas.types.ck` alone are over 150 and every one of them is
# trailing documentation. A 150-column ceiling and a house style of long trailing
# `#` prose cannot both hold, and the prose is the part worth keeping — these are
# the source of the routers, the types and the SDK, and they are read far more
# often than they are edited.
#
# Not a bug report: the plugin round-trips these files (see the formatter notes
# in `.claude/skills/contractkit/SKILL.md`, which track what it used to eat). It
# reformats correctly and the result is less readable, which is a different
# complaint and one only an ignore file can answer.
**/*.ck
